# Copy this file to .env, next to the config.toml you run against, and fill in the
# value. .env is gitignored by a glob that also covers .env.bak and .env.local; this
# file is the one deliberate exception, and it documents the variable name without
# documenting anybody's key.
#
# The name is not fixed. This tool reads whatever [model].api_key_env in your
# config.toml names, so a config that says api_key_env = "MY_GATEWAY_KEY" wants
# MY_GATEWAY_KEY here instead. OPENROUTER_API_KEY is what both shipped examples
# name. See docs/configuration.md, under [model], for the whole rule, including
# which wins when the same variable is already exported in your shell.
#
# A platform credential goes here the same way, under whatever name your config
# gives it: [source].credential_env for reading comments, [publish].credential_env
# for sending an approved reply. They may be two names or one, and a config that
# names only the first can read and cannot publish anything at all.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
